    {
      "title": "Comparisons and alternatives",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "CDC event processing decouples work from the original database transaction; Salesforce’s example uses the change event rather than the original object to start its Apex-to-Flow bridge. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://developer.salesforce.com/blogs/2021/01/calling-flow-from-cdc-events",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:88efd3c920b9e1b79b084cb8d547f370dc8b945ea36176a11e8f5396cf8ec75d",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:0332c7360a8fe09c8b6a59c1652408676160b25793492147cd2a07bde5d94ff4",
            "ev:3baba2d9fecf13f18b0ae4bac9a875cd79004b867f8dc28bccf754737117f4a0"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Outbound-message retries can arrive out of order or more than once. Check notification IDs before processing. If the source record changes while the notification is queued, delivery contains the latest data rather than intermediate changes, so this mechanism cannot provide an audit trail. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/api/guide/sforce-api-om-outboundmessaging-notifications.html",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:4ede4b0b9b2f0237dbe98704b7e36f4ddcef7a31e230145854a7261bab205e8b",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:9b7fd212dceca1195608bb9066890f1f89df19561c24f0c0486984e687e333d5",
            "ev:d74baefe88523dab971d3be915e5771293b0551716f287e6987c20ec1aff6110"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://help.salesforce.com/s/articleView?id=000386475&language=en_US&type=1"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Facts and statements",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Asynchronous Salesforce processing has no completion-time SLA or consistent latency guarantee. An external case alert design therefore needs an explicit latency expectation and monitoring. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://architect.salesforce.com/docs/architect/fundamentals/guide/async-fundamentals",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:cca0a4789f8a72714af1ed7376797047fd4273d86e20528ff703f368da427c04",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:1d7597f173246aab3d7bb61f15e36ee46c5c111af75b894f107fa3415128fc97",
            "ev:71e911eb633d4a4c9cdca663c3d8b595eca2600ef27500f08b29bb415505199a"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "If a SOAP outbound-message endpoint is unavailable, Salesforce retries delivery and drops the message after 24 hours of unsuccessful delivery. This is bounded retry, not indefinite guaranteed delivery. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-12)",
          "source": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/api/guide/sforce-api-om-outboundmessaging-notifications.html",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:980aa7be229a9bc725a5e002b4825d68399f832876549b3838047e98f2da43fb",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
