      "text": "Apex can bridge CDC events to Flow, separating automation from the original save transaction. Flow HTTP callouts depend on transaction boundaries. After-save Flow can also initiate SOAP outbound messages, whose background delivery has bounded retries, duplicates, ordering limitations, and latest-value payloads. These properties matter when choosing an external case-alert path and defining monitoring and latency expectations. The CDC-to-Flow example is historical; it does not establish current direct CDC-trigger support in Flow.",
